            <ArticleTitle>[The effect of alcohol consumption on carboxypeptidase N activity in rat brain during chronic emotional-painful stress].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With ethanol consumption, activity of carboxypeptidase H was increased in all the brain regions of rats with chronic emotional-painful stress. The most distinct increase of enzyme activity was found in the striatum membrane fraction and in the hippocampus. Carboxypeptidase H appears to be involved in development of stress reactions under conditions of ethanol consumption via the enkephalinergic system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
